  "history_notes": [
    "[INVENTED] Window E533500 N181850 to E534700 N179850 on EPSG:27700, 48x80 cells of 25 m, y=0 to the north (D-093); drawn from data/maps/sources/whitechapel_full_sources.csv and .md (Chronicler, #201), +-1 cell.",
    "[INVENTED] Streets are the simplified centre lines of the sources, two cells wide (D-086): each cell a line crosses marks its whole 2x2 street piece. Back streets are left out.",
    "[INVENTED] Wapping sin calles por alcance del hito: Wapping High Street existía en 1866.",
    "[INVENTED] The two halves of Commercial Road (1806 east of Back Church Lane, the western extension of 1865 or 1870) are joined at y 21 across the 3-cell gap of the sources.",
    "[INVENTED] Each Thames stairs runs south as a column of stairs from its cell down to the river, so it meets the water; stairs are no land to build on, no street and no river (D-094).",
    "[DEBATED] Parish lines are drawn by hand along the boundary streets (+-1-2 cells). The south tip of Spitalfields and the City edge are folded into Whitechapel, Wellclose and East Smithfield into St George in the East, the St Katharine precinct and the Tower riverside into Wapping.",
    "[INVENTED] Land the dock outlines leave shut in, with only a dock around it, is dock: a 9-cell notch inside the Western Dock (32-40, 56) and a 5-cell sliver between it and the east edge (47, 54-58).",
